From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:21:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/23] rocket: rk3576: cut the CPU cost of an invoke

 - NHWC <-> NC1HWC2 conversion walked pixel by pixel, so the host tensor
   is read or written strictly sequentially and each 16-byte group is one
   NEON load, XOR and store; signed inputs no longer need a flipped copy.
 - A subgraph input BO is only read by the NPU and fully rewritten on
   every invoke, so it is mapped write-only unsynchronized and the
   PREP_BO wait and cache invalidate are skipped (the FINI_BO clean at
   unmap stays).
 - The submit jobs of a subgraph are the same on every invoke; build them
   once and keep them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
